body:
Before, we had some CSS in place to prevent submitting empty comments. That worked well as  when using a mouse, but you can still submit empty comments via keyboard—AFAIK there's not a keyboard-equivalent to `pointer-events: none`.

This PR sprinkles in some JS to properly disable the Submit button if there's nothing in the textarea (or only whitespace).

@jorgemanrubia, I wonder if something like this might be nice to bake into Lexxy?

So that navigation shortcuts work

@dhh we could inject the shortcuts in the markup so that they work without loading the menu, but the current approach is nice because it keeps them together and consistent with the shortcut we show on each button. This menu does not change accross screens, so I think HTTP caching should work well here.

I will merge this so that we fix the problem with shorcuts. I can restore lazy loading if you think it is important. My call would be to wait to make sure it is justified.

To avoid any visual flashes of the old theme before the Stimulus controllers load, we can apply the saved theme from `<head>` whenever there is a full page load.

This applies to both the regular and public views, as we're doing it in the shared head partial.

@jzimdars @andyra what do you think -- worth it or no? The difference is mostly only noticeable on first load or refresh.
